============================================================================================
the operator is non-monotone, which is why there is no canonical fixpoint
============================================================================================
  site holds {CARRIER}                -> W recoverable: False  ACCESS recoverable: False
  site holds {CARRIER, STRIDE}        -> W recoverable: True   ACCESS recoverable: True
  ACCESS is an output when the site holds {CARRIER} and is NOT one when it holds
  {CARRIER, STRIDE}. so growing O REMOVES a member of O. a monotone operator cannot
  do that, and lfp/gfp are therefore unavailable as a tie-break between the fixpoints.

distinct criterion-consistent output sets across all 16 cells: 7
   |O| = 0   {}
   |O| = 2   {ACCESS, CARRIER}
   |O| = 2   {CARRIER, STRIDE}
   |O| = 3   {ACCESS, CARRIER, COMPUTE}
   |O| = 3   {ACCESS, CARRIER, STRIDE}
   |O| = 3   {CARRIER, COMPUTE, STRIDE}
   |O| = 4   {ACCESS, CARRIER, COMPUTE, STRIDE}

